  <entry>
    <id>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/16/2026-21146/implementation-of-electronic-submission-of-mariner-course-completion-data#2026-10-16</id>
    <title>Final rule: Implementation of Electronic Submission of Mariner Course Completion Data</title>
    <link href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/16/2026-21146/implementation-of-electronic-submission-of-mariner-course-completion-data"/>
    <updated>2026-10-16T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Notification. This document announces that the Coast Guard will not require the electronic submission requirement for mariner course completion data until at least November 25, 2028, because the system for providing the electronic submission is not yet fully operational. The Coast Guard will notify the public through the Federal Register before requiring the electronic submission of course completion data. Affects 46 CFR 10. Comments close 2028-11-25.</summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/01/2026-20087/clarification-of-certain-mariner-training-requirements#2026-10-01</id>
    <title>Proposed rule: Clarification of Certain Mariner Training Requirements</title>
    <link href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/01/2026-20087/clarification-of-certain-mariner-training-requirements"/>
    <updated>2026-10-01T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Notice of proposed rulemaking. The Coast Guard proposes removing six requirements related to endorsements for the International Convention on Standards of Training, Certification, and Watchkeeping for Seafarers, 1978, as amended, and the Seafarer&apos;s Training, Certification, and Watchkeeping Code. Changes would affect Masters and Officers in Charge of a Navigational Watch of less than 500 GT in near-coastal waters; Officers in Charge of an Engineering Watch, Designated Duty Engineers, and Electro-technical Ratings of 750 kW/1,000 HP or more. This proposed action includes technical revisions to remove duplicative or outdated language from the regulatory text, reduces regulatory burdens, and promotes equivalent compliance standards with international requirements. Affects 46 CFR 11, 46 CFR 12. Comments close 2026-12-30.</summary>
  </entry>
